  "title": "On the Chain-of-Thought Monitorability of Looped Language Models",
  "summary": "This report investigates the monitorability of CoT reasoning in LoopLMs, which are designed to handle deep reasoning by repeating shared transformer layers. The study reveals that while LoopLMs can increase computational depth, they also raise concerns about reduced CoT faithfulness and monitorability in certain tasks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "This paper provides the first systematic evaluation of CoT monitorability in LoopLMs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study isolates the effect of additional recurrent computation by varying the loop depth within the same model.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The comparison of LoopLMs with non-looped models shows no evidence of systematic lower monitorability.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
